{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1549 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "13732c223b57c79c0c4b8943d97429cbf7bd30fb8823cee2402dbb53151c4781" :edb/db-before-t 1548 :edb/db-after-t 1549 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534861 50 #inst "2026-10-08T09:23:18.915Z" 13194139534861 true] [17592186124131 1100 "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet  $\\dfrac{(x-3)^2}9 + \\dfrac{(y+4)^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(z-5)^2}{25} = 1,$ find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." 13194139534861 true] [17592186124131 1100 "Given the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\dfrac{(x-3)^2}9 + \\dfrac{(y+4)^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(z-5)^2}{25} = 1$, find its intercepts with the $x$-axis." 13194139534861 false] [17592186124131 1145 "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n((x - 3)^{2})/(9) + ((0 + 4)^{2})/(16) - ((0 - 5)^{2})/(25) &= 1 \\\\\n((x - 3)^{2})/(9) + 1 - 1 &= 1 \\\\\n((x - 3)^{2})/(9) &= 1 \\\\\n(x - 3)^{2} &= 9 \\\\\nx - 3 &= ± \\sqrt{9} \\\\\nx &= 3 ± 3 \\\\\nx &= 0, 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(6,0,0)$." 13194139534861 false] [17592186124131 1145 "To find the $x$-intercepts, we plug $y=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(0+4)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{(0-5)^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+1-1 & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9} & =1 \\\\ (x-3)^{2} & =9 \\\\ x-3 & =\\pm \\sqrt{9} \\\\ x & =3\\pm 3 \\\\ x & =0,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $x$-axis are $(0,0,0)$ and $(6,0,0).$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186124227 1100 "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $(x-1)^2 + y^2 - \\dfrac{z^2}{4} = -1$, find the domain of $z = z(x,y)$." 13194139534861 false] [17592186124227 1100 "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $(x-1)^2 + y^2 - \\dfrac{z^2}{4} = -1,$ find the domain of $z = z(x,y).$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186124227 1145 "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(x - 1)^{2} + y^{2} - \\frac{z^{2}}{4} &= -1 \\\\\n(x - 1)^{2} + y^{2} + 1 &= \\frac{z^{2}}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{z^{2}}{4} &= (x - 1)^{2} + y^{2} + 1 \\\\\nz^{2} &= 4((x - 1)^{2} + y^{2} + 1) \\\\\nz &= ± 2\\sqrt{(x - 1)^{2} + y^{2} + 1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2$, we have\n\n$$\n(x-1)^2 + y^2 + 1 \\geq 0\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is $\\mathbb R^2$." 13194139534861 false] [17592186124227 1145 "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1 & =\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{2}}{4} & =(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =4((x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1) \\\\ z & =\\pm 2\\sqrt{(x-1)^{2}+{y}^{2}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in\\mathbb R^2,$ we have\n\n$$\n(x-1)^2 + y^2 + 1 \\geq 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is $\\mathbb R^2.$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186124282 1100 "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets\n$-\\dfrac{(x-5)^2}{8} + \\dfrac{y^2}{50} + (z-3)^2 = -1$\nand the plane $z = 4$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" 13194139534861 false] [17592186124282 1100 "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of two sheets \n\n$$\n-\\dfrac{(x-5)^2}{8} + \\dfrac{y^2}{50} + (z-3)^2 = -1\n$$\n\nand the plane $z = 4$ onto the $xy$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" 13194139534861 true] [17592186124282 1145 "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $z = 4$, we substitute $z = 4$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n- ((x - 5)^{2})/(8) + \\frac{y^{2}}{50} + (z - 3)^{2} &= -1 \\\\\n&= - ((x - 5)^{2})/(8) + \\frac{y^{2}}{50} + 1 =-1 \\\\\n- ((x - 5)^{2})/(8) + \\frac{y^{2}}{50} &= -2 \\\\\n((x - 5)^{2})/(8) - \\frac{y^{2}}{50} &= 2 \\\\\n((x - 5)^{2})/(16) - \\frac{y^{2}}{100} &= 1 \\\\\n((x - 5)^{2})/(4^{2}) - \\frac{y^{2}}{10^{2}} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $10$." 13194139534861 false] [17592186124282 1145 "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $z = 4,$ we substitute $z = 4$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}+(z-3)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}+1=-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50} & =-2 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50} & =2 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{16}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{100} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{{4}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{10}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $4$ and $10.$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186124421 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315615 13194139534861 true] [17592186124421 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315622 13194139534861 true] [17592186124421 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315629 13194139534861 true] [17592186124421 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315664 13194139534861 true] [17592186124476 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315636 13194139534861 true] [17592186124476 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315643 13194139534861 true] [17592186124476 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315657 13194139534861 true] [17592186124571 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315587 13194139534861 true] [17592186124571 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315594 13194139534861 true] [17592186124571 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315601 13194139534861 true] [17592186124571 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315608 13194139534861 true] [17592186124571 1020 #edb/ref 17592186315650 13194139534861 true] [17592186124743 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534861 true] [17592186124743 1100 "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $x^{2} + y^{2} - z^{2} =-1$, find the domain of $z = z(x, y)$." 13194139534861 false] [17592186124743 1100 "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2}=-1$, find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186124743 1145 "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-{z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+1 & ={z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2} & =1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2} \\\\ {z}^{2} & =\\pm \\sqrt{1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n1+{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}\\ge 1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is ${R}^{2}.$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186124798 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534861 true] [17592186124798 1100 "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{x^{2}}{8} + ((y - 4)^{2})/(18) - \\frac{z^{2}}{50} = 1$ and the plane $x = 2$ onto the $yz$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" 13194139534861 false] [17592186124798 1100 "The projection of the intersection between the hyperboloid of one sheet $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50}=1$ and the plane $x=2$ onto the $yz$-plane is a hyperbola. What are the lengths of the semi-axes of the hyperbola?" 13194139534861 true] [17592186124798 1145 "To find the intersection of the hyperboloid and the plane $x=2$, we substitute $x=2$ into the equation of the hyperboloid:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(2)^{2}}{8}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =1-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{18}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{50} & =\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{25} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{(y-4)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us the equation of a hyperbola with semi-axes of lengths $3$ and $5.$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315587 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315588 13194139534861 true] [17592186315587 1089 "q-164272" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315587 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534861 true] [17592186315587 1100 "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{4}=-1,$ find its $z$-intercepts." 13194139534861 true] [17592186315587 1113 #uuid "b589cdc8-22e6-5881-b7f2-9fb3725db0fb" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315587 1145 "To find the $z$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $y=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{0}^{2}+\\frac{{0}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ -\\frac{(z+1)^{2}}{4} & =-1 \\\\ (z+1)^{2} & =4 \\\\ z+1 & =\\pm 2 \\\\ z & =-1\\pm 2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $z=-3$ and $z=1.$\n\nTherefore, the intercepts with the $z$-axis are $(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,1).$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315589 13194139534861 true] [17592186315588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315590 13194139534861 true] [17592186315588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315591 13194139534861 true] [17592186315588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315592 13194139534861 true] [17592186315588 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315593 13194139534861 true] [17592186315588 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534861 true] [17592186315588 1041 "selection" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315588 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315590 13194139534861 true] [17592186315588 1110 #uuid "86e1a9ed-4f62-57a1-98dd-46c3510dd0fb" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315589 1034 "$(0,0,-3)$ only" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315589 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534861 true] [17592186315589 1111 #uuid "7c1f33a3-5a7d-5250-8690-d0b1e2b31503" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315590 1034 "$(0,0,-3)$ and $(0,0,1)$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315590 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534861 true] [17592186315590 1111 #uuid "4602829c-92f6-5884-85b8-f5cd2580da68" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315591 1034 "$(0,0,-2)$ and $(0,0,2)$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315591 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534