true] [17592186315608 1113 #uuid "754f0d41-0427-55a9-9b96-3f7987630b52" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315608 1145 "To find the $y$-intercepts, we plug $x=0$ and $z=0$ into the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(0+3)^{2}}{3}+\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{5}-(0-1)^{2} & =-1 \\\\ 3+\\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{5}-1 & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{(y+6)^{2}}{5} & =-3 \\\\ (y+6)^{2} & =-15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis equation has no (real) solutions.\n\nTherefore, the hyperboloid does not intersect the $y$-axis." 13194139534861 true] [17592186315609 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315610 13194139534861 true] [17592186315609 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315611 13194139534861 true] [17592186315609 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315612 13194139534861 true] [17592186315609 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315613 13194139534861 true] [17592186315609 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315614 13194139534861 true] [17592186315609 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534861 true] [17592186315609 1041 "selection" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315609 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315610 13194139534861 true] [17592186315609 1110 #uuid "c5c03aa5-28e4-5a21-a736-39184c27e49c" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315610 1034 "The hyperboloid does not intersect the $y$-axis" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315610 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534861 true] [17592186315610 1111 #uuid "2eb07d56-3fa3-5046-8d3b-2ecd39381c73" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315611 1034 "$(0,-3,0)$ and $(0,3,0)$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315611 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534861 true] [17592186315611 1111 #uuid "bee3f268-6375-5654-b9aa-d74100e20baa" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315612 1034 "$(0,-6+\\sqrt{5},0)$ only" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315612 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534861 true] [17592186315612 1111 #uuid "b90b3c75-ca9e-5fb2-86f8-480b6344bec3" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315613 1034 "$(0,-6,0)$  only" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315613 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534861 true] [17592186315613 1111 #uuid "2c9b0369-4c6b-539a-98e9-68f48bdf129b" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315614 1034 "$(0,-6+\\sqrt{5},0)$ and $(0,-6-\\sqrt{5},0)$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315614 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534861 true] [17592186315614 1111 #uuid "c2924483-de99-5fd9-8578-e1c1438b78e8" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315615 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315616 13194139534861 true] [17592186315615 1089 "q-164303" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315615 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534861 true] [17592186315615 1100 "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}=-1,$ find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315615 1113 #uuid "c07acc0b-9718-5922-85a6-2aa92546197c" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315615 1145 "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =-1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1 & =\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{z}^{2}}{16} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1 \\\\ {z}^{2} & =16(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1) \\\\ z & =\\pm 4\\sqrt{\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}+1\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is ${R}^{2}.$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315617 13194139534861 true] [17592186315616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315618 13194139534861 true] [17592186315616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315619 13194139534861 true] [17592186315616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315620 13194139534861 true] [17592186315616 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315621 13194139534861 true] [17592186315616 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534861 true] [17592186315616 1041 "selection" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315616 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315618 13194139534861 true] [17592186315616 1110 #uuid "58f1d285-3a06-59c2-853f-912821471ec6" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315617 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}>1}" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315617 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534861 true] [17592186315617 1111 #uuid "e920d31d-d868-512e-93de-35bbf89ca31e" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315618 1034 "{R}^{2}" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315618 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534861 true] [17592186315618 1111 #uuid "08d0290f-39d9-5388-9902-0bda8462709b" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315619 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\le 1}" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315619 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534861 true] [17592186315619 1111 #uuid "1f2f473e-a26c-58b0-8e23-5f9fa69c15b0" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315620 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}<1}" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315620 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534861 true] [17592186315620 1111 #uuid "701b5a8f-c4b8-5cd5-8b15-8019b2c65537" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315621 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}\\ge 1}" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315621 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534861 true] [17592186315621 1111 #uuid "a344b2d5-7c8c-51c5-940c-9cd4376e0446" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315622 1017 #edb/ref 17592186315623 13194139534861 true] [17592186315622 1089 "q-164305" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315622 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534861 true] [17592186315622 1100 "Given the hyperboloid of two sheets ${x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}-{z}^{2}=-1,$ find the domain of $z=z(x,y).$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315622 1113 #uuid "5bb2562b-5a93-5104-a36a-5ac52a24497a" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315622 1145 "From the hyperboloid equation, we make $z$ the subject as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}-{z}^{2} & =-1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}+1 & ={z}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{z}^{2} & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}+1 \\\\ z & =\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square root is defined only for non-negative arguments. However, notice that for all $(x,y)\\in {R}^{2},$ we have\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}+1\\ge 0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the domain of $z(x,y)$ is ${R}^{2}.$" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315624 13194139534861 true] [17592186315623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315625 13194139534861 true] [17592186315623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315626 13194139534861 true] [17592186315623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315627 13194139534861 true] [17592186315623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186315628 13194139534861 true] [17592186315623 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534861 true] [17592186315623 1041 "selection" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315623 1104 #edb/ref 17592186315624 13194139534861 true] [17592186315623 1110 #uuid "916737dc-253b-516e-8eda-5ec6902712f2" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315624 1034 "{R}^{2}" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315624 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534861 true] [17592186315624 1111 #uuid "d5aa9d4f-aef4-5c27-8f83-c947cd135b80" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315625 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}<1}" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315625 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534861 true] [17592186315625 1111 #uuid "a457dae7-a9ac-560c-be31-22d5c368546a" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315626 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}\\le 1}" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315626 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534861 true] [17592186315626 1111 #uuid "474c85e9-6d21-52c7-9dff-b9ad74f044b0" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315627 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}>1}" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315627 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534861 true] [17592186315627 1111 #uuid "099178e4-39cb-532a-8676-55508c397851" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315628 1034 "{(x,y)\\,:\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{(y-3)^{2}}{9}\\ge 1}" 13194139534861 true] [17592186315628 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534861 true] [17592186315628